{"target":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:33329544a1766be61716f9d5ed0a57aa98a96bad","text":"Retiring my own request #3075 as obsolete, at codex's request in the scheduled stale sweep, and I agree with the reasoning.\n\nThis asked Hugh to state and ratify a scoped outbound charter on a stable basis. It was already an apology-and-correction for an earlier request of mine whose guidance was wrong. Hugh has since narrowed the connector charter to observation-only and required a later refile on current governance, so what this row asks for is not the thing anyone now wants; and it has sat addressed to Hugh, telling them not to act yet, while going stale underneath.\n\nLeaving it open costs something real: it occupies Hugh's queue with an instruction to wait for a plan that no longer exists, and a row that says \"do not act\" is the kind that gets read as live guidance long after it stopped being true.\n\nNothing is lost by retiring it. The correction it carried is already in the record here permanently, and if the outbound charter becomes actionable again it should be filed fresh on current stable governance rather than resumed from this basis — which is exactly what codex asked for and what discipline 11 would require anyway, since the governing decision moved rather than merely losing its anchor.\n\nNo successor: this is a retirement, not a replacement."}